/* Manu Tere · zh · pack nz · generated by build.py; loaded with the pack */
__mtLangPack('zh','nz',{"Right ▶":"右 ▶","Soil scrubbed off, {A} / 5.":"泥土已刷掉，{A} / 5。","Not a crumb of soil left. Now the spray.":"一点泥土也不剩了。现在来喷一喷。","Sprayed. Your boots carry no soil into the forest.":"喷好了。你的靴子不会把泥土带进森林。","The forest of <b>Waipoua</b>, home of the great kauri trees. At the entrance stands a cleaning station. <b>Kauri dieback</b>, a disease that lives in the soil, is spread on muddy shoes and kills kauri. <b>Scrub every bit of soil off your boots</b>, then spray them.":"<b>Waipoua</b> 森林，巨大的贝壳杉（kauri）的家园。入口处有一个清洁站。<b>贝壳杉枯梢病</b>是一种生活在土壤里的病害，会随着沾泥的鞋子传播，并会杀死贝壳杉。<b>把靴子上的泥土刷得一点不剩</b>，然后喷一喷。","On the boardwalk, a muddy little shortcut leads between the roots to a better photo spot.":"木栈道上，有一条泥泞的小捷径从树根之间穿过，通往一个更好的拍照点。","Take the shortcut, just once":"走捷径，就一次","The roots of a kauri lie just under the soil: one step can hurt them, and carry the disease.":"贝壳杉的根就在土壤下面：踩一步就可能伤到它们，还会传播病害。","Yes: the boardwalk keeps your feet off the roots.":"对：木栈道让你的脚远离树根。","Your friend wants to hug a kauri for luck.":"你的朋友想抱一抱贝壳杉，求个好运。","Walk up to the trunk and hug it":"走到树干前抱住它","To reach the trunk you would stand on its roots.":"要走到树干前，你就得踩在它的根上。","Admire it from the boardwalk":"在木栈道上欣赏它","Yes: the roots spread far around the trunk.":"对：树根在树干周围伸展得很远。","You have finished your apple.":"你吃完了苹果。","Throw the core into the ferns, it is natural":"把果核扔进蕨丛里，反正是天然的","Food scraps do not belong in the forest.":"食物残渣不属于森林。","Keep the core and take it home":"留着果核，带回家","Yes: leave nothing behind.":"对：什么都不留下。","Here he is: <b>Tāne Mahuta</b>, named after Tāne, who in Māori tradition is the god of forests and birds. <b>Look up</b>: his trunk rises with no branch for more than {#1} m.":"他就在这里：<b>Tāne Mahuta</b>，以 Tāne 命名——在毛利传统中，Tāne 是森林与鸟类之神。<b>抬头看</b>：他的树干笔直向上，超过 {#1} m 都没有一根树枝。","Shout to hear the echo":"大喊一声，听听回声","Stand quietly a moment on the platform, and listen to the birds":"在平台上静静站一会儿，听鸟儿歌唱","Yes. A tūī answers from the canopy.":"对。一只 tūī 从树冠上回应了你。","Quiet is the respect this place asks for.":"安静，就是这个地方所要求的尊重。","Why must visitors clean their shoes before entering a kauri forest?":"为什么游客进入贝壳杉森林前必须清洁鞋子？","To stop kauri dieback, a disease carried in soil":"为了阻止贝壳杉枯梢病，一种通过土壤传播的病害","Yes: clean shoes and staying on the boardwalk protect the trees.":"对：干净的鞋子和留在木栈道上，都能保护这些树。","To keep the boardwalk shiny":"为了让木栈道保持锃亮","It is about the trees, not the boards.":"这关乎树木，而不是木板。","Because the forest is a museum":"因为森林是一座博物馆","It is a living forest: the soil carries the danger.":"这是一片活的森林：危险藏在土壤里。","In the forest of Waipoua you scrubbed and sprayed your boots, stayed on the boardwalk, took your apple core home, and stood quietly before Tāne Mahuta, {#1} m tall.":"在 Waipoua 森林里，你刷洗并喷洒了靴子，留在木栈道上，把苹果核带回了家，还静静地站在 {#1} m 高的 Tāne Mahuta 面前。","Kupe chases the great octopus of Muturangi far from Hawaiki, across the ocean.":"Kupe 追赶 Muturangi 的巨型章鱼，从 Hawaiki 出发，一路横渡大洋。","He ao!":"He ao!","Kuramārōtini, Kupe’s wife, sees a long white cloud on the sea: land!":"Kupe 的妻子 Kuramārōtini 看见海上有一朵长长的白云：陆地！","Kupe travels the coasts and gives names to places.":"Kupe 沿着海岸航行，为各地取名。","From this harbour Kupe sails home: Te Hokianga-nui-a-Kupe, the place of his great return.":"Kupe 从这个港湾启程回家：Te Hokianga-nui-a-Kupe，他伟大归程之地。","Not yet: what happens before that?":"还没到：在那之前发生了什么？","At the mouth of the Hokianga, an elder tells the story of <b>Kupe</b>, the great navigator. Some traditions say it like this; other iwi tell it differently. <b>Tap the four parts of the story in order.</b>":"在 Hokianga 河口，一位长者讲述伟大航海家 <b>Kupe</b> 的故事。有些传统这样讲述；其他部落（iwi）的说法不同。<b>按顺序点击故事的四个部分。</b>","The harbour is called <b>Te Hokianga-nui-a-Kupe</b>. What does the name remember?":"这个港湾名叫 <b>Te Hokianga-nui-a-Kupe</b>。这个名字纪念的是什么？","The place of Kupe’s great return":"Kupe 伟大归程之地","The place where Kupe fought the octopus":"Kupe 与章鱼搏斗之地","The place where Kupe was born":"Kupe 出生之地","Yes: hoki means to return. From here Kupe went home, some traditions say to Hawaiki.":"对：hoki 的意思是返回。Kupe 从这里回家，有些传统说是回到了 Hawaiki。","Listen to the word hoki: to go back.":"听听 hoki 这个词：回去。","In the story, what did Kuramārōtini see first?":"在故事里，Kuramārōtini 最先看到了什么？","A long white cloud on the sea":"海上一朵长长的白云","Yes: he ao tea roa, linked to the name Aotearoa.":"对：he ao tea roa，与 Aotearoa 这个名字有关。","A great octopus":"一只巨型章鱼","The octopus was what Kupe chased.":"章鱼是 Kupe 追赶的对象。","No lighthouse in Kupe’s time.":"Kupe 的时代可没有灯塔。","At the mouth of the Hokianga you put Kupe’s story in order, as some traditions tell it: the octopus, the long white cloud, the names, and the great return that gave the harbour its name.":"在 Hokianga 河口，你按照有些传统的讲法，把 Kupe 的故事排好了顺序：章鱼、长长的白云、命名，以及让港湾得名的伟大归程。","Opononi, the summer of {#1}. A wild dolphin, a young female the town calls <b>Opo</b>, comes to play with the swimmers in the harbour, and people come from all over the country to see her. <b>Which of these keep Opo safe?</b>":"Opononi，{#1} 年夏天。一只野生海豚——镇上人叫她 <b>Opo</b> 的年轻雌海豚——来到港湾里和游泳的人玩耍，全国各地的人都赶来看她。<b>以下哪些做法能保护 Opo 的安全？</b>","Stand still in the water and let her come to you":"在水中站着不动，让她自己游过来","Chase her to touch her fin":"追着她去摸她的鳍","Throw her pieces of fish":"扔鱼块给她吃","Safe for Opo":"对 Opo 安全","Not for Opo":"对 Opo 不安全","Yes: a wild dolphin chooses when to come close.":"对：野生海豚会自己决定什么时候靠近。","Right: chasing and feeding change a wild dolphin’s life, and can hurt her.":"没错：追逐和投喂会改变野生海豚的生活，还可能伤害她。","Think of what a wild animal needs.":"想想野生动物需要什么。","Boats cross the harbour all day. You help a skipper: <b>tap Slow</b> each time Opo swims close to the boat, so the propeller cannot hurt her. Three times.":"船只整天在港湾里来来往往。你在帮一位船长：每当 Opo 游近船边，就<b>点击“减速”</b>，这样螺旋桨就不会伤到她。共三次。","Slow and steady: Opo is safe, {A} / 3.":"慢而稳：Opo 很安全，{A} / 3。","She is far from the boat for now.":"她现在离船还很远。","In {#1} something new happened for Opo. What?":"{#1} 年，Opo 身上发生了一件新鲜事。是什么？","A law was passed to protect her in the harbour":"通过了一项在港湾里保护她的法律","She was taken to an aquarium":"她被送进了水族馆","She learned to talk":"她学会了说话","Dolphins whistle and click, but no.":"海豚会吹口哨、发出咔嗒声，但不会说话。","At Opononi you learned how to keep a wild dolphin safe: stand still and let her come, no chasing and no feeding, and slow the boat whenever Opo swam close, as the law of {#1} wanted.":"在 Opononi，你学会了如何保护野生海豚的安全：站着不动让她过来，不追逐、不投喂，每当 Opo 游近就让船减速，正如 {#1} 年那项法律所要求的。","Corn on the cob":"玉米棒","Kūmara, sweet potato":"Kūmara，红薯","A pumpkin":"一个南瓜","Ice cream":"冰淇淋","A tin of beans, closed":"一罐没开的豆子","A basket of corn, kūmara and pumpkin.":"一篮玉米、kūmara 和南瓜。","Ice cream would melt in the steam!":"冰淇淋在蒸汽里会融化的！","A closed tin can burst in the heat: never.":"密封的罐头受热会爆开：千万不要。","What cooks the food in the steam boxes of Whakarewarewa?":"Whakarewarewa 的蒸汽箱是靠什么把食物蒸熟的？","Steam from the hot ground":"来自炽热地下的蒸汽","Yes: the heat of the earth, every day.":"对：大地的热量，天天如此。","A gas stove hidden inside":"藏在里面的燃气灶","No stove: the ground does the work.":"没有炉灶：是大地在干活。","The heat comes from below.":"热量来自下方。","The valley of <b>Te Puia</b> and Whakarewarewa: boiling mud, hot pools and, on its white terrace, <b>Pōhutu</b>, the great geyser. The boardwalk goes between the vents; the fences keep you on the cool side. <b>Step</b> along the boardwalk, but <b>wait</b> while steam blows across it.":"<b>Te Puia</b> 与 Whakarewarewa 山谷：沸腾的泥浆、温泉池，还有在白色台地上的大间歇泉 <b>Pōhutu</b>。木栈道在喷气孔之间穿行；围栏让你待在凉爽的一侧。沿着木栈道<b>前进</b>，但蒸汽飘过栈道时要<b>等待</b>。","Steam on the boardwalk: wait until it clears.":"蒸汽飘到了木栈道上：等它散开。","At the viewpoint, behind the rail.":"到观景点了，在栏杆后面。","Pōhutu at full height, {A} / 2.":"Pōhutu 喷到了最高，{A} / 2。","Wait for the jet to rise.":"等水柱升起来。","A visitor climbs over the fence to touch the white terrace for a better photo. What do you tell him?":"一名游客翻过围栏，想摸一摸白色台地，好拍张更好的照片。你对他说什么？","Quick, before the guide sees":"快点，趁向导还没看见","Come back: the crust can be thin over boiling water, and new vents open without warning":"回来：沸水上面的地壳可能很薄，新的喷气孔会毫无预警地出现","Yes. The fences are where the ground is safe.":"对。有围栏的地方，才是地面安全的地方。","Off the boardwalk the ground can give way into boiling water.":"离开木栈道，地面可能塌陷，掉进沸水里。","In a geothermal valley, where is it safe to walk?":"在地热山谷里，在哪里行走才安全？","On the boardwalks and paths, behind the fences":"在木栈道和小路上，在围栏后面","Yes: that is where the ground has been checked.":"对：那些地方的地面都经过检查。","Anywhere the ground looks white and hard":"任何看起来又白又硬的地方","A white crust can hide boiling water.":"白色的地壳下面可能藏着沸水。","Close to the vents, to feel the warmth":"靠近喷气孔，感受温暖","Steam burns, and vents can erupt.":"蒸汽会烫伤人，喷气孔也会喷发。","In the valley of Te Puia you crossed the boardwalk between the steaming vents, waiting when the steam blew across, photographed Pōhutu at full height, and called a visitor back behind the fence.":"在 Te Puia 山谷里，你走过冒着蒸汽的喷气孔之间的木栈道，蒸汽飘过时耐心等待，拍下了喷到最高的 Pōhutu，还把一名游客叫回了围栏后面。","Over, under, over: the strips hold each other tight.":"上、下、上：叶条彼此紧紧咬住。","At Te Puia, students of the national weaving school work with <b>harakeke</b>, New Zealand flax, to make <b>kete</b>, baskets, and much more. They let you try the simplest weave, over and under. Each tap lays a pale strip <b>over</b> the green one. <b>Copy the pattern</b> on the right.":"在 Te Puia，国家编织学校的学生用 <b>harakeke</b>（新西兰麻）编织 <b>kete</b>（篮子）等许多东西。他们让你试试最简单的编法：一上一下。每点击一次，就把一根浅色叶条压在绿色叶条<b>上面</b>。<b>照着右边的图案编</b>。","Which plant do weavers use for kete, the woven baskets?":"编织者用哪种植物来编 kete（编织篮）？","Yes: its long, strong leaves are split into strips.":"对：它又长又结实的叶子会被劈成细条。","Pine needles":"松针","Too short and brittle.":"太短，也太脆。","Kauri bark":"贝壳杉树皮","The kauri is protected, and not a weaving plant.":"贝壳杉受到保护，而且不是编织用的植物。","At Te Puia you watched the weavers and wove a little square of harakeke, over and under, matching the pattern strip by strip.":"在 Te Puia，你观看了编织者工作，还用 harakeke 一上一下地编了一小块方格，一条一条地对上了图案。","Pull gently":"轻轻拉","Without flash it is fine":"不开闪光灯就没关系","No photos at all in here: just look, and remember":"这里完全不能拍照：只用眼睛看，用心记住","Yes. No photos or video at all, even without flash, and quiet in the boat.":"对。完全不能拍照或录像，即使不开闪光灯也不行，在船上还要保持安静。","The rule here is no photos at all, flash or not.":"这里的规定是完全不能拍照，开不开闪光灯都一样。","Why do visitors keep quiet in the glow-worm grotto?":"为什么游客在萤火虫洞里要保持安静？","To hear the guide’s radio":"为了听清向导的收音机","There is no radio: silence is the point.":"根本没有收音机：重点就是安静。","Because the cave is closed":"因为洞穴关闭了","It is open, with a guide.":"洞穴是开放的，有向导带领。","At Waitomo you pulled the boat along the wire with slow, quiet pulls{A}, drifted under thousands of glow-worms, and kept your phone in your pocket.":"在 Waitomo，你用缓慢安静的动作沿着钢索拉船{A}，从成千上万只萤火虫下面漂过，手机一直放在口袋里。","Now its two <b>Pointers</b>, the bright stars that lead the eye to the Cross: tap them.":"现在找它的两颗<b>指极星</b>，就是把视线引向十字的亮星：点击它们。","The Pointers, Alpha and Beta Centauri.":"指极星，南门二和马腹一。","Matariki: a new year begins when it rises before dawn.":"Matariki：它在黎明前升起时，新的一年就开始了。","The larva of a small fly, which glows to catch insects in sticky threads":"一种小蝇的幼虫，它发光是为了用黏丝捕捉昆虫","Yes: its light lures tiny insects into the silk threads it hangs.":"对：它的光把小昆虫引到它垂下的丝线上。","A tiny star fallen into the cave":"一颗掉进洞里的小星星","A lovely idea, but it is an insect.":"想法很美，但它是一种昆虫。","A glowing mushroom":"一种会发光的蘑菇","No: it moves, and it eats.":"不是：它会动，也会吃东西。","Too late: a fingerprint of oil stays on the stone.":"太晚了：石头上留下了一个带油的指纹。","Hand back in the pocket, {A} / 3.":"手放回口袋了，{A} / 3。","No one is touching anything right now.":"现在没有人在碰东西。","Why does the guide ask everyone not to touch?":"为什么向导要求大家都不要触摸？","The stone is very hot":"石头非常烫","The oil of our skin stains the stone and stops it growing, and the formations grow very slowly":"我们皮肤上的油脂会弄脏石头、让它停止生长，而这些岩石长得非常慢","They break like glass at a touch":"它们一碰就像玻璃一样碎掉","Yes. A touch takes a second; the damage lasts for centuries.":"对。触摸只需一秒；损害却会持续几个世纪。","Think of what our hands leave behind.":"想想我们的手会留下什么。","Who cares for the Waitomo caves today, with the company that runs the tours?":"如今，除了经营游览的公司，还有谁在照管 Waitomo 洞穴？","The descendants of the original Māori owners, to whom the land was returned in {#1}":"原毛利土地所有者的后代，这片土地在 {#1} 年归还给了他们","Yes: the families of Tāne Tinorau and the other owners.":"对：Tāne Tinorau 和其他所有者的家族。","No one: caves look after themselves":"没有人：洞穴会照顾自己","Caves need care: lights, paths, rules.":"洞穴需要照管：灯光、步道、规则。","A team of scientists in Europe":"欧洲的一支科学家团队","No: the owners are local families.":"不是：所有者是当地的家族。","In the caves of Waitomo you stopped {A} hands from touching the stalactites{B}, learned why the oil of our skin harms them, and who the land belongs to.":"在 Waitomo 的洞穴里，你阻止了 {A} 只手去摸钟乳石{B}，了解了为什么我们皮肤上的油脂会伤害它们，也知道了这片土地属于谁。","Here he is: <b>Tāne Mahuta</b>, “Lord of the Forest”, named after Tāne, who in Māori tradition is the god of forests and birds. <b>Look up</b>: his trunk rises with no branch for more than {#1} m.":"他就在这里：<b>Tāne Mahuta</b>，“森林之王”，以 Tāne 命名——在毛利传统中，Tāne 是森林与鸟类之神。<b>抬头看</b>：他的树干笔直向上，超过 {#1} m 都没有一根树枝。","{#1} m from the roots to the top of the crown, {#2} m around the trunk: the largest known living kauri, perhaps {#3} to {#4} years old.":"从根部到树冠顶端 {#1} m，树干周长 {#2} m：已知现存最大的贝壳杉，树龄也许有 {#3} 到 {#4} 年。","Keep calm and keep your hands to yourself":"保持平静，手不要乱碰","Yes: on {#1} March {#2}. Sadly, Opo died the very next day; the town buried her with honours, and her statue with a child still stands at Opononi.":"对：在 {#2} 年 3 月 {#1} 日。令人难过的是，Opo 第二天就死了；镇上的人为她举行了隆重的葬礼，她和一个孩子的雕像至今仍立在 Opononi。","No: she was a wild dolphin and lived free in the harbour.":"不：她是野生海豚，在港湾里自由自在地生活。","In the living village of <b>Whakarewarewa</b>, home of Tūhourangi Ngāti Wāhiao, families cook with the heat of the earth: in <b>steam boxes</b> built over the vents, and in the boiling pools. Your guide shows you how the village cooks. <b>Help choose what goes in the flax basket</b>: three things to steam.":"在 <b>Whakarewarewa</b> 这个活的村落里——Tūhourangi Ngāti Wāhiao 的家园——家家户户用大地的热量做饭：用建在地热喷气孔上的<b>蒸汽箱</b>，或者用沸腾的水池。你的向导给你演示村里是怎么做饭的。<b>帮忙挑选放进新西兰麻篮子里的东西</b>：三样可以蒸的东西。","<b>Stand back</b>: the guide lifts the wooden lid, and hot steam rushes out. Only the guide goes near the box. When you are a safe step away, the guide lowers the basket and closes the lid.":"<b>往后站</b>：向导掀开木盖，热气一下子冲了出来。只有向导才能靠近蒸汽箱。等你退到安全的距离，向导就把篮子放进去，盖上盖子。","Now wait. The steam does the cooking. <b>Tell the guide when you think the kai is ready</b>: watch the steam, and the colour of the timer.":"现在等着。蒸汽会把食物蒸熟。<b>你觉得 kai 好了，就告诉向导</b>：留意蒸汽，还有计时器的颜色。","It’s ready!":"好了！","The guide shakes her head: the kūmara is still hard.":"向导摇摇头：kūmara 还是硬的。","The guide lifts the lid: very soft, but still good, the steam is gentle.":"向导掀开盖子：很软了，但还是好吃，蒸汽很温和。","The guide lifts the lid: perfect, soft, sweet and smelling of the earth.":"向导掀开盖子：完美，软糯香甜，带着大地的气息。","Your hosts hand you a share of the kai. What do you do?":"主人递给你一份 kai。你会怎么做？","Start eating without a word":"一句话不说就开吃","Thank your hosts for the kai: kia ora":"感谢主人的 kai：kia ora","You are a guest: thank the people who fed you.":"你是客人：要感谢给你食物的人。","In the living village of Whakarewarewa you chose corn, kūmara and pumpkin for the flax basket, stood back while the guide steamed it over the vents, told her when it was ready, and thanked your hosts for the kai.":"在 Whakarewarewa 这个活的村落里，你为新西兰麻篮子挑选了玉米、kūmara 和南瓜，在向导用喷气孔的蒸汽蒸煮时站在一旁，告诉她什么时候熟了，并感谢了主人的 kai。","Pōhutu erupts up to {#1} times a day, sometimes up to {#2} m high. <b>Take a photo at the top of the jet</b>: two good photos.":"Pōhutu 每天最多喷发 {#1} 次，有时高达 {#2} m。<b>在水柱最高点拍照</b>：拍两张好照片。","<b>Waitomo</b>: the stream that runs into the ground. In {#1} Tāne Tinorau and Fred Mace followed it into the cave on a raft. Today the guide pulls the boat by hand along a wire, in the dark: bright light and noise disturb the glow-worms, so the grotto is kept dark and silent. <b>Pull the wire gently</b>: slow, steady pulls, no splashing.":"<b>Waitomo</b>：流入地下的溪流。{#1} 年，Tāne Tinorau 和 Fred Mace 乘着木筏顺着溪流进入了洞穴。如今，向导在黑暗中沿着一根钢索用手拉船前进：强光和噪音会打扰萤火虫（发光蕈蚊幼虫），所以洞里一直保持黑暗和安静。<b>轻轻拉动钢索</b>：慢慢地、稳稳地拉，不要溅起水花。","Splash! The guide raises a finger: silence in the grotto.":"哗啦！向导竖起一根手指：洞里要保持安静。","Bright light and noise disturb the glow-worms, so the grotto is kept dark and silent":"强光和噪音会打扰萤火虫，所以洞里一直保持黑暗和安静","Yes: so the boat is pulled silently, by hand, in the dark.":"对：所以船是在黑暗中靠人手静静地拉着走的。","Last, a tight little cluster: <b>Matariki</b>, the Pleiades, whose rising in midwinter marks the Māori new year for many iwi; some look to Puanga instead. In Tahiti it is Matariʻi. <b>Tap its nine lights.</b>":"最后，是一个紧凑的小星团：<b>Matariki</b>，昴星团，对许多部落（iwi）来说，它在仲冬时节升起，标志着毛利新年；也有些部落看的是 Puanga。在塔希提，它叫 Matariʻi。<b>点击它的九个光点。</b>","Before the boat ride, the guide lights the <b>Cathedral</b>, the high chamber of the cave, and the slow shapes of limestone: stalactites hang from the roof, stalagmites rise from the floor, a drop at a time over thousands of years. Visitors are tempted to touch them. <b>Tap Hands off!</b> when a hand reaches for a formation. Three times.":"坐船之前，向导点亮了<b>大教堂</b>——洞穴里高大的洞厅——还有石灰岩缓慢形成的形状：钟乳石从洞顶垂下，石笋从地面升起，一滴一滴，历经数千年。游客们很想去摸。每当有手伸向这些岩石时，<b>点击“别碰！”</b>。共三次。","Te Roroa, the iwi of this land, are the guardians of the forest, together with the Department of Conservation. Many visitors like to greet Tāne Mahuta. How?":"Te Roroa 是这片土地的部落（iwi），他们与新西兰保护部一起守护着这片森林。很多游客喜欢向 Tāne Mahuta 致意。怎么做呢？","Yes. Hosts care for their guests with food; guests say thank you.":"对。主人用食物款待客人；客人则说声谢谢。","◀ bend":"◀ 弯道","bend ▶":"弯道 ▶","Above the lake, the <b>Skyline Luge</b>: a gondola up the hill, then a three-wheeled cart with no motor, down winding tracks, since {#1}. <b>Push</b> to roll, <b>Brake</b> before a bend, and <b>hold Left or Right</b> to lean into it. Helmet on? Then go.":"在湖的上方，是 <b>Skyline Luge</b>（Skyline 滑车）：先坐缆车上山，再坐一辆没有马达的三轮滑车，沿着弯弯曲曲的赛道滑下来，从 {#1} 年起就是如此。<b>推</b>一下就能滑动，弯道前<b>刹车</b>，并<b>按住左或右</b>来侧身入弯。头盔戴好了吗？那就出发。","No helmet, it spoils my hair":"不戴头盔，会弄乱我的头发","Helmet on, strap tight":"戴上头盔，系紧带子","Helmet on. Children under {#1} or under {#2} cm ride with an adult.":"戴上头盔。{#1} 岁以下或身高不足 {#2} cm 的孩子要和大人一起乘坐。","No helmet, no ride: those are the rules.":"不戴头盔就不能玩：这是规定。","Down the track. Brake <b>before</b> each bend and lean the right way; too fast into a bend and the cart slides off onto the grass.":"沿着赛道往下滑。每个弯道<b>之前</b>要刹车，并朝正确的方向侧身；入弯太快，滑车就会滑出赛道冲上草地。","Smooth through the bend.":"顺利过弯。","Off onto the grass! Brake before the bend, and lean into it.":"冲上草地了！弯道前要刹车，并侧身入弯。","Leaned the wrong way: onto the grass.":"侧身方向错了：冲上草地。","At the bottom, the chairlift takes you and the cart back up for another run. On the chair, what do you do?":"到了山脚，缆椅把你和滑车一起送回山上，再滑一次。坐在缆椅上，你会怎么做？","Swing the chair and lean out for a photo":"摇晃缆椅，探出身子拍照","Sit back, bar down, cart hooked on, feet still":"靠着坐好，放下安全杆，挂好滑车，脚不乱动","Yes. A chairlift is calm or it is nothing.":"对。坐缆椅就要安安静静，否则就不要坐。","No swinging: the chair is high above the trees.":"不要摇晃：缆椅高高悬在树梢之上。","How does a luge cart slow down?":"滑车是怎么减速的？","The rider pulls the handlebar back: the brakes work by hand":"乘坐者把车把往后拉：刹车靠手来控制","Yes: push to go, pull to brake, lean to steer. No motor.":"对：推就走，拉就刹，侧身转向。没有马达。","It has a motor that reverses":"它有一个可以倒转的马达","No motor at all: gravity does the work.":"完全没有马达：全靠重力。","It does not: you wait for the bottom":"它不会减速：等到底就行了","You brake before every bend.":"每个弯道前你都要刹车。","without leaving the track":"，没有滑出赛道","On the Skyline Luge you put your helmet on, rode six bends down the hill{A}, and sat still on the chairlift back up.":"在 Skyline 滑车上，你戴上头盔，滑过六个弯道下了山{A}，并在回山上的缆椅上坐得稳稳的。","The boat glides into the <b>Glowworm Grotto</b>: thousands of tiny blue-green lights above the black water. Beside you a visitor takes out a phone for a photo, without flash. What do you whisper?":"小船滑进了<b>萤火虫洞</b>：成千上万个蓝绿色的小光点悬在漆黑的水面上方。你身旁一位游客掏出手机想拍照，不开闪光灯。你小声说什么？","The Southern Cross, made of glow-worms.":"南十字座，由萤火虫组成。","In the dark, the glow-worms look like a night sky. Out of the boat, the guide whispers: “Can you find the stars that brought the waka here?” <b>Tap the four lights of the Southern Cross</b>: the long bar and the short one.":"在黑暗中，萤火虫看起来就像夜空。下了船，向导轻声问：“你能找到把 waka 带到这里的星星吗？”<b>点击南十字座的四个光点</b>：长的一条和短的一条。","What is a glow-worm?":"萤火虫是什么？","Under the glow-worms of Waitomo you traced the Southern Cross, its two Pointers and the nine lights of Matariki, the stars of the voyagers and of the Māori new year.":"在 Waitomo 的萤火虫下，你描出了南十字座、它的两颗指极星，以及 Matariki 的九个光点——它们是航海者之星，也是毛利新年之星。","Rangitoto, the volcano island":"Rangitoto，火山岛","The Waitematā harbour and its ferries":"Waitematā 港湾和它的渡轮","The harbour bridge":"海港大桥","Part of the floor is <b>glass, {#1} mm thick</b>: you look straight down {#2} m to the street. Your friend is scared to step on it. What do you say?":"地板有一部分是<b>玻璃，{#1} mm 厚</b>：你可以直直地往下看到 {#2} m 下面的街道。你的朋友不敢踩上去。你会说什么？","Jump on it to show it holds":"在上面跳几下，证明它撑得住","It is as strong as the concrete beside it: step on it when you feel ready, or walk round":"它和旁边的混凝土一样结实：准备好了再踩上去，或者绕着走","Yes. Nobody is pushed; the view is there for everyone.":"对。谁也不会被逼着上去；风景属于每一个人。","No jumping on the glass, and no pushing a friend.":"不要在玻璃上跳，也不要逼朋友。","The <b>SkyWalk</b>: a ring outside the tower, {#1} m up, {#2} m wide, <b>no handrail</b>. First the harness and the overhead safety line. <b>Clip in</b>: both clips.":"<b>SkyWalk</b>：塔外的一圈环形走道，离地 {#1} m，宽 {#2} m，<b>没有扶手</b>。先穿好安全带，接上头顶的安全绳。<b>挂好</b>：两个挂钩都要挂上。","Clip the harness":"挂上安全带","Clip the safety line":"挂上安全绳","One clip. And the other.":"挂好一个。还有另一个。","Walk round the ring, <b>one step at a time</b>. When the wind gusts, the guide says <b>stop</b>: wait for it to pass, then go on. Eight steps.":"绕着环形走道走，<b>一步一步来</b>。刮起阵风时，向导会说<b>停</b>：等风过去，再继续走。共八步。","STOP · wind":"停 · 有风","Wait: a gust. Hold still until the guide says go.":"等一下：一阵风。站稳别动，直到向导说可以走。","All the way round, {#1} m above the city.":"绕了整整一圈，在城市上空 {#1} m 处。","Why do the Sky Tower lifts sometimes slow down or stop?":"Sky Tower 的电梯为什么有时会减速或停下来？","Sensors feel the tower sway in strong wind, and slow the lifts for safety":"传感器感应到大风中塔身的摇晃，为了安全让电梯减速","Yes: in a big wind the lifts even return to the ground and wait.":"对：风很大的时候，电梯甚至会回到地面等着。","To save electricity":"为了省电","No: it is about the wind.":"不：是因为风。","Because too many people are inside":"因为里面的人太多了","The lifts count the wind, not the people.":"电梯在意的是风，不是人数。","At the top of the Sky Tower you found Rangitoto, the harbour, the bridge and Ōkahu Bay, respected your friend on the glass floor, clipped in twice and walked the SkyWalk ring, stopping for every gust.":"在 Sky Tower 顶上，你找到了 Rangitoto、港湾、大桥和 Ōkahu 湾，在玻璃地板上尊重了朋友的选择，挂好两个挂钩走完了 SkyWalk 环形走道，每遇阵风就停下来。","A seed stuck in the sole of your shoe":"一颗卡在鞋底的种子","Mud caked on the other shoe":"另一只鞋上结块的泥","An ant in a fold of the bag":"包的褶缝里的一只蚂蚁","A bottle of water":"一瓶水","A torch for the lava caves":"一支去熔岩洞用的手电筒","A seed out: one seed can start a weed on a whole island.":"种子取出来了：一颗种子就能让杂草蔓延整座岛。","Mud brushed off: soil carries seeds and disease.":"泥刷掉了：土壤会带着种子和病害。","The ant shaken out: no new insects for Rangitoto.":"蚂蚁抖掉了：不给 Rangitoto 带去新的昆虫。","Keep the water: you will need it.":"水留着：你会需要它。","Keep the torch: the lava caves are dark.":"手电筒留着：熔岩洞里很黑。","<b>Rangitoto</b> rose out of the sea only about {#1} years ago: the youngest volcano of Auckland, {#2} minutes by ferry from the city. It is kept free of rats and other pests, so every visitor <b>checks, cleans and seals</b> their bag. <b>Take out what must not come ashore.</b>":"<b>Rangitoto</b> 大约 {#1} 年前才从海里升起：它是奥克兰最年轻的火山，从市区乘渡轮 {#2} 分钟可达。岛上没有老鼠和其他有害生物，所以每位游客都要<b>检查、清理并封好</b>自己的包。<b>把不能上岸的东西拿出来。</b>","The summit track: {#1} km there and back, {#2} m up over black lava, through the largest pōhutukawa forest in the world. <b>Walk</b> in a steady rhythm; stop in the shade when you are hot.":"登顶步道：往返 {#1} km，在黑色熔岩上爬升 {#2} m，穿过世界上最大的 pōhutukawa 森林。<b>走</b>的时候保持稳定的节奏；热了就在树荫下停一停。","The summit: all of Auckland and the gulf below you.":"山顶：整个奥克兰和海湾都在你脚下。","Fifteen minutes from the summit, the <b>lava caves</b>: tunnels the lava left as it drained away, dark, with low ceilings. <b>Switch on your torch</b> and tap the three places to light.":"离山顶十五分钟，是<b>熔岩洞</b>：熔岩流走时留下的隧道，黑暗，洞顶很低。<b>打开手电筒</b>，点击三个地方把它们照亮。","Low ceiling: duck your head.":"洞顶很低：低头。","The lava left ropes and ripples on the rock.":"熔岩在岩石上留下了绳状和波纹状的痕迹。","Daylight ahead: the way out.":"前面有天光：出口。","Why do visitors check and clean their bags before Rangitoto?":"去 Rangitoto 之前，游客为什么要检查和清理自己的包？","The island is kept free of pests, soil and weed seeds":"岛上要保持没有有害生物、泥土和杂草种子","Yes: rats were removed, and the birds and plants depend on it staying that way.":"对：老鼠已经被清除，鸟类和植物都靠这一点来生存。","Because the ferry is small":"因为渡轮很小","It is about the island, not the boat.":"是为了岛，不是为了船。","To find their ticket":"为了找船票","Tickets are easy: seeds and ants are the problem.":"船票好找：种子和蚂蚁才是问题。","On Rangitoto you took the seed, the mud and the ant out of your bag, climbed the young volcano in a steady rhythm, and lit your torch through the lava caves.":"在 Rangitoto，你把种子、泥和蚂蚁从包里清了出去，以稳定的节奏登上了年轻的火山，并打着手电筒穿过了熔岩洞。","Right at the water’s edge, in front of everyone, for the best photo":"就站在水边，在所有人前面，拍最好的照片","Behind the hosts, where the visitors are shown to stand":"站在主人后面，游客被安排站的地方","Yes. The front of the beach belongs to the hosts and the crews.":"对。海滩的前排属于主人和船员。","Not in front: this welcome is theirs, you are a guest.":"不要站在前面：这场欢迎是他们的，你是客人。","The canoes come closer. The welcome begins: calls, speeches, songs, in te reo Māori and in Hawaiian. It lasts a long time. <b>What do you do?</b>":"独木舟越来越近。欢迎仪式开始了：呼喊、致辞、歌唱，用毛利语和夏威夷语。仪式持续很长时间。<b>你会怎么做？</b>","Talk with your friend about lunch":"和朋友聊午饭吃什么","Quiet: the words are the point, even those you do not understand.":"安静：这些话才是重点，即使你听不懂。","Walk across the beach to see the canoes from the side":"穿过海滩，从侧面看独木舟","Nobody crosses between the hosts and their guests.":"谁也不能从主人和客人之间穿过。","Stand still, listen, and wait until the hosts say the welcome is over":"站着不动，用心听，等主人宣布欢迎仪式结束","Yes. A welcome has an order; guests follow it to the end.":"对。欢迎仪式有它的顺序；客人要跟到最后。","The welcome is over; people mix on the beach, and the crews answer questions. A crew member tells you the canoes sailed <b>from Rarotonga in {#1} days</b>, without instruments, like Kupe. Someone offers you food. What do you say?":"欢迎仪式结束了；人们在海滩上交谈，船员们回答问题。一位船员告诉你，独木舟<b>从 Rarotonga 出发，用了 {#1} 天</b>，不靠任何仪器，就像 Kupe 一样。有人请你吃东西。你会说什么？","Nothing, and eat":"什么也不说，直接吃","Kia ora, thank you":"Kia ora，谢谢","Kia ora: hello, and thank you.":"Kia ora：你好，也是谢谢。","Two words go a long way: kia ora.":"两个词就很管用：kia ora。","Where did Hōkūleʻa sail from to reach Aotearoa in November {#1}?":"{#1} 年 11 月，Hōkūleʻa 是从哪里出发抵达 Aotearoa 的？","From Rarotonga, in the Cook Islands":"从库克群岛的 Rarotonga","Yes: the same way as your manu, Kupe’s way.":"对：和你的 manu 走的是同一条路，Kupe 之路。","From Sydney":"从悉尼","No: from the east, across the open ocean.":"不：是从东边，横渡开阔的大洋。","From Antarctica":"从南极洲","Far too cold for a canoe.":"对独木舟来说太冷了。","At Ōkahu Bay you watched the voyaging canoes come in from Rarotonga, stood where the visitors stand, stayed quiet through the whole welcome, and said kia ora for the food.":"在 Ōkahu 湾，你看着远航独木舟从 Rarotonga 驶来，站在游客该站的地方，整场欢迎仪式都保持安静，并为食物说了 kia ora。","Missed a gate: look further down the slope.":"漏了一个旗门：眼睛看向坡道更远处。","You passed {A} gates of 10. The weather turns: cloud comes down and the wind rises, as it often does on Ruapehu. What do you do?":"10 个旗门你通过了 {A} 个。天气变了：云压下来，风刮起来，Ruapehu 上常常这样。你会怎么做？","Go higher, above the cloud, for one last run":"爬到更高处、云层之上，再滑最后一趟","Follow the instructor back to the base, and put on every warm layer":"跟着教练回到基地，把所有保暖衣物都穿上","Yes. Storms have trapped skiers on this mountain overnight: back to the base, warm and together.":"对。暴风雪曾把滑雪者整夜困在这座山上：回基地去，保暖，大家待在一起。","In cloud you cannot see the lifts or the edges: never higher alone.":"在云里你看不见缆车，也看不见坡道边缘：千万不要一个人往更高处去。","Ruapehu is a sacred mountain and an active volcano. Where may a visitor go?":"Ruapehu 是一座圣山，也是一座活火山。游客可以去哪里？","Anywhere, it is a park":"哪里都行，这是公园","Down into the crater lake to swim":"下到火口湖里游泳","Clean! A 360 and a flat landing, {A} / 3.":"漂亮！转了 360 度，平稳落地，{A} / 3。","Too early: wait for the lip.":"太早了：等到跳台边缘。","Too late: you rode over the jump.":"太晚了：你从跳台上滑过去了。","A smaller child has fallen in the landing zone of the jump, just below the lip. What do you do?":"一个更小的孩子摔在了跳台的着陆区，就在边缘下方。你会怎么做？","Jump anyway, you will clear her":"照样跳，你能越过她","Stop, cross your board above the jump as a signal, and help her out of the landing":"停下，把滑雪板横放在跳台上方作为信号，然后帮她离开着陆区","Yes. Nobody drops in while the landing is not clear.":"对。着陆区没清空，谁也不能下跳台。","You cannot see the landing from the lip: never jump blind.":"从跳台边缘看不见着陆区：千万不要盲跳。","When is the snow season at Whakapapa, in the southern hemisphere?":"在南半球的 Whakapapa，雪季是什么时候？","From late June to late October":"从六月底到十月底","Yes: winter in the south, when it is summer in Europe.":"对：南半球的冬天，正是欧洲的夏天。","From December to March":"从十二月到三月","That is the southern summer: no snow then.":"那是南半球的夏天：那时没有雪。","All year round":"一年四季","The snow melts in summer.":"夏天雪会化掉。","without a fall":"，一次也没摔","SLOW · end of the run":"减速 · 滑道终点","In <b>Happy Valley</b> a magic-carpet lift takes sledges to the top of a gentle slope. <b>Hold Left or Right</b> to steer round the cones, and <b>Brake</b> with your heels before the end of the run.":"在 <b>Happy Valley</b>，魔毯传送带把雪橇送到一个缓坡的顶上。<b>按住左或右</b>绕过雪锥，并在滑道终点前用脚后跟<b>刹车</b>。","Heels in the snow: stopped before the fence.":"脚后跟插进雪里：在栅栏前停住了。","Not yet: brake near the red line.":"还没到：在红线附近刹车。","Bumped a cone! Steer earlier.":"撞到雪锥了！要早一点转向。","Into the soft snow bank at the end: next time, brake at the red line.":"冲进了终点的软雪堆：下次在红线处刹车。","Why do skiers on Ruapehu carry warm clothes and a little food even for a short run?":"在 Ruapehu 滑雪的人，为什么哪怕只滑一小段也要带着保暖衣物和一点食物？","The weather can change fast, and storms have trapped people on the mountain":"天气可能变得很快，暴风雪曾把人困在山上","Yes: cloud, wind and snow can close the road in an hour.":"对：云、风和雪能在一小时内让道路封闭。","For a picnic at the crater lake":"为了在火口湖边野餐","The crater lake is tapu and dangerous: no picnic there.":"火口湖是 tapu，而且很危险：不能在那里野餐。","Because the café is expensive":"因为咖啡馆太贵了","It is about safety on a high mountain.":"这是为了高山上的安全。","braked at the red line before the fence":"在栅栏前的红线处刹住了车","learned to brake at the red line":"学会了在红线处刹车","Tāmaki Makaurau, Auckland. The <b>Sky Tower</b> rises {#1} m to the tip of its mast: for {#2} years the tallest structure in the southern hemisphere, until a tower in Jakarta passed it in {#3}. The lift takes you to the main deck at {#4} m. <b>Find four places</b> in the view.":"Tāmaki Makaurau，奥克兰。<b>Sky Tower</b>（天空塔）高 {#1} m，直到桅杆的顶端：它曾在 {#2} 年里是南半球最高的建筑，直到 {#3} 年被雅加达的一座塔超过。电梯把你送到 {#4} m 高的主观景层。<b>在景色中找出四个地方</b>。","The <b>SkyWalk</b>: a ring outside the tower, {#1} m up, {#2} m wide, <b>no handrail</b>. It is for ages {#3} and up. First the harness and the overhead safety line. <b>Clip in</b>: both clips.":"<b>SkyWalk</b>：塔外的一圈环形走道，离地 {#1} m，宽 {#2} m，<b>没有扶手</b>。{#3} 岁及以上才能参加。先穿好安全带，接上头顶的安全绳。<b>挂好</b>：两个挂钩都要挂上。","Clipped in twice: the line holds you. Now walk.":"两个都挂好了：安全绳拉着你。现在走吧。","<b>Ōkahu Bay</b>, {#1} November {#2}. The voyaging canoes <b>Hōkūleʻa</b> and <b>Hikianalia</b>, come from Hawaiʻi by way of Tahiti and Rarotonga, sail into the bay. The people of this place, Ngāti Whātua Ōrākei, welcome the crews on the beach. You are a visitor among the crowd. <b>Where do you stand?</b>":"<b>Ōkahu 湾</b>，{#2} 年 11 月 {#1} 日。远航独木舟 <b>Hōkūleʻa</b> 和 <b>Hikianalia</b> 从 Hawaiʻi 出发，经由 Tahiti 和 Rarotonga，驶进了海湾。这片土地的主人 Ngāti Whātua Ōrākei 在海滩上迎接船员。你是人群中的一名游客。<b>你站在哪里？</b>","<b>Whakapapa</b>, on the north side of Ruapehu, {#1} m up: the largest ski field of Aotearoa, open from late June to late October. In <b>Happy Valley</b>, the beginners’ slope, your instructor sets a slalom. <b>Hold Left or Right</b> to steer through the gates: ten gates.":"<b>Whakapapa</b>，位于 Ruapehu 的北侧，海拔 {#1} m：Aotearoa 最大的滑雪场，从六月底开放到十月底。在初学者坡道 <b>Happy Valley</b>，你的教练设了一条回转滑雪赛道。<b>按住左或右</b>来穿过旗门：共十个旗门。","On the ski field and its marked trails; the peaks are tapu, and iwi ask visitors not to stand on them":"滑雪场和标好的雪道；山峰是 tapu，部落（iwi）请游客不要站上去","Yes. In {#1} Te Heuheu Tūkino IV placed the peaks under protection so they could never be sold; the crater lake is hot and acid, and erupted in {#2} while people were on the ski field.":"对。{#1} 年，Te Heuheu Tūkino IV 把这些山峰置于保护之下，使它们永远不能被出售；火口湖又热又酸，并在 {#2} 年人们还在滑雪场上时喷发过。","No: the peaks are sacred, and the mountain is an active volcano.":"不：山峰是神圣的，而且这座山是一座活火山。","Never: the lake is hot and acid, and the peaks are tapu.":"绝对不行：湖水又热又酸，而且山峰是 tapu。","In Happy Valley at Whakapapa you skied the slalom ({A} gates of 10), came down with the instructor when the cloud closed in, and left the peaks and the crater lake alone.":"在 Whakapapa 的 Happy Valley，你滑了回转赛道（10 个旗门通过了 {A} 个），云压下来时跟着教练下了山，并且没有去碰山峰和火口湖。","The <b>jumps</b>: a few kickers shaped in the snow for boards. Your coach says: bend your knees, <b>tap Jump exactly at the lip</b> of the kicker (when the white ramp reaches your board), spin once, and land flat. Three jumps.":"<b>跳台</b>：几座在雪里为滑雪板塑形的跳台。教练说：屈膝，<b>正好在跳台的边缘点击“跳”</b>（当白色坡道碰到你的滑雪板时），转一圈，平稳落地。共三跳。","At Waitomo you pulled the boat along the wire with slow, quiet pulls, drifted under thousands of glow-worms, and kept your phone in your pocket.":"在 Waitomo，你沿着钢索慢慢地、静静地拉船前行，从成千上万只萤火虫下漂过，手机一直放在口袋里。","At Waitomo you pulled the boat along the wire with slow, quiet pulls, without a single splash, drifted under thousands of glow-worms, and kept your phone in your pocket.":"在 Waitomo，你沿着钢索慢慢地、静静地拉船前行，没有溅起一点水花，从成千上万只萤火虫下漂过，手机一直放在口袋里。","In the caves of Waitomo you stopped three hands from touching the stalactites, learned why the oil of our skin harms them, and who the land belongs to.":"在 Waitomo 的洞穴里，你拦住了三只想去摸钟乳石的手，了解了皮肤上的油脂为什么会伤害它们，也知道了这片土地属于谁。","In the caves of Waitomo you stopped every hand in time from touching the stalactites, learned why the oil of our skin harms them, and who the land belongs to.":"在 Waitomo 的洞穴里，你及时拦住了每一只想去摸钟乳石的手，了解了皮肤上的油脂为什么会伤害它们，也知道了这片土地属于谁。","On the Skyline Luge you put your helmet on, rode six bends down the hill, visited the grass once or twice, and sat still on the chairlift back up.":"在 Skyline 滑车上，你戴好头盔，一路下山过了六个弯，还去草地上逛了一两次，回程的缆椅上也坐得稳稳的。","On the Skyline Luge you put your helmet on, rode six bends down the hill without leaving the track, and sat still on the chairlift back up.":"在 Skyline 滑车上，你戴好头盔，一路下山过了六个弯，没有滑出赛道，回程的缆椅上也坐得稳稳的。","On the jumps you landed three times, and stopped to help a fallen child before anyone dropped in.":"在跳台上你三次成功落地，并在有人起跳之前停下来，帮助了一个摔倒的孩子。","On the jumps you landed three times without a fall, and stopped to help a fallen child before anyone dropped in.":"在跳台上你三次成功落地、一次都没摔，并在有人起跳之前停下来，帮助了一个摔倒的孩子。","In Happy Valley you steered the sledge round the cones, bumping one or two, and braked at the red line before the fence.":"在 Happy Valley，你驾着雪橇绕过锥桶，撞到了一两个，并在栅栏前的红线处刹住了车。","In Happy Valley you steered the sledge round the cones, bumping one or two, and learned to brake at the red line.":"在 Happy Valley，你驾着雪橇绕过锥桶，撞到了一两个，并学会了在红线处刹车。","In Happy Valley you steered the sledge round every cone and braked at the red line before the fence.":"在 Happy Valley，你驾着雪橇绕过了每一个锥桶，并在栅栏前的红线处刹住了车。","In Happy Valley you steered the sledge round every cone and learned to brake at the red line.":"在 Happy Valley，你驾着雪橇绕过了每一个锥桶，并学会了在红线处刹车。"});
